  "body": "**Main does not compile** (from 51979785, through 7f0928fe). Three PRs that each built alone collided once merged:\n\n1. **#783 (motion onto Stock)** made `quality::measure` return `Result<PathQuality, StockError>`, and `stock_for` return a `Stock` instead of a `Dexel`. The trochoidal slot (#563/#778) still:\n   - read `q.max_deg` and `q.max_at` on the bare result (`trochoid_slot.rs`);\n   - passed the stock to `lifted_cut`, which took `&mut Dexel` (`trochoid_air.rs`).\n2. **The #697 approach law** (`origin_approach::no_generator_seeds_the_clearance_plane_without_the_approach_law`) found the trochoid's `finish()` seeding with `PathBuilder::new` at X0 Y0 on the clearance plane.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`trochoid_slot.rs`:** both `measure` calls go through one `gauge` closure that maps the stock error to a named `GenError` (\"trochoidal slot: measuring stock: …\", the wording the `stock()` closure already uses). The lifted-return read maps its error the same way. `finish()` seeds with `PathBuilder::approached`. Its first move is already a rapid, so the path is unchanged.\n- **`trochoid_air.rs`:** `lifted_cut` takes `&mut Stock` and returns `Result<Option<Point3>, StockError>`. It cuts with `Stock::subtract_flat` (the same column-arm law as `Dexel::subtract`) and reads through `Columns::col`/`top_at`. A stock the reading can't serve is an error, never a pass.\n- **`tests/trochoid_slot.rs`:** the two test call sites read the `Result`.\n\n**How tested (Linux):**\n- **The batch gate** on 2c05183c: geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, app (including the slow lane), ui and clippy all ok. Motion's one failure was `origin_approach` (item 2 above), fixed in 0f96b56b.\n- **On 0f96b56b:**\n  - the quick gate (motion suites 131 s, app) is green;\n  - `origin_approach::no_generator_seeds_the_clearance_plane_without_the_approach_law` is green;\n  - the `trochoid_slot` suite is green, including `trochoid_microlift_returns_land_on_air` (the lifted-return law still catches a return over uncut stock).\n\n**Not exercised:** a GUI trochoid run. The law tests cover the behaviour.\n\nChangelog: none (restores the build; no behaviour change from the released state)\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\n\nFixes #844\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
